{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"beaten-reluctant-anole","creation_channel":"python","description":"Scope: root-level `src/rebar/*.py` plus `attest/`, `metrics/`, `review_bot/`, `opcert_service/`, `audit/`, `grounding/`, `_guides/`. ~180 lines leave of 7,248 comment lines (2.5%) — this scope is in good health and the yield is concentrated, not diffuse.\n\nSURFACED A LIVE DEFECT, filed separately: `_mcp_models.BridgeFsckOut` omits `binding_drift`, so the MCP outputSchema under-declares a field `bridge_fsck.py:217` always returns. The comment at `_mcp_models.py:31-34` claiming 'the cross-interface schema tests pin both to the canonical schema' is FALSE — those model names appear zero times in tests/. That false assurance is why the drift went unnoticed.\n\nTwo prior leads resolved AGAINST the hypothesis and belong in do_not_move: `_mcp_llm.py`'s 121 docstring lines are the literal wire-visible MCP tool descriptions FastMCP publishes to clients — API surface, not narration, zero recoverable. And `_config_schema.py`'s `# read-via:` markers are machine-consumed by `scripts/check_config_reads.py`, a CI gate — deleting one breaks CI.\n\nCaveat that bounds this shard: 280 of `_config_schema.py`'s 792 lines are comments, and for many keys they are the ONLY documentation — `docs/config.md` has zero coverage for `completion_floor_active`, `comment_max_chars`, `auth_proxy_secret_env`. Recovering more than ~34 lines there requires writing those doc rows FIRST, or the trim destroys documentation rather than relocating it.\n\nThree new ADRs proposed from `review_bot/`: bounded shutdown (drain/cancel/grace-period chain, test-pinned against docker-compose `stop_grace_period`); the deploy-safe in-flight counter and its deliberate over-count; retryable coverage gaps deferring vote-less under a bounded budget.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Every non-KEEP unit in scope is relocated or deleted per its destination [operator-attested]\n- [x] The shard's do_not_move list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` BEFORE any edit lands\n- [x] Verified-stale comments are corrected where they document a live invariant, deleted only where obsolete\n- [x] No load-bearing invariant is lost\n## CORRECTION (plan-review preempt, parent 373f disposition vocabulary)\n\nSuperseding ACs encode the 373f disposition rules and the verified state of this shard's claims.\nKEY UPDATE: the shard's headline \"SURFACED A LIVE DEFECT\" is now STALE — that defect has already\nbeen fixed on main (BridgeFsckOut now declares `binding_drift`, `_mcp_models.py` now correctly\ncites the CI-enforced drift gate `python -m rebar.schemas.check_mcp_models --check`, and the\n`test_mcp_model_schema_drift_*` tests now exist). So that comment is CORRECT-AS-IS → DO_NOT_MOVE,\nNOT a correction target. The two documentation-load-bearing do_not_move findings are confirmed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (supersedes the list above)\n\n- [x] Every substantial in-scope comment unit is dispositioned into exactly one parent-373f\n      label: RELOCATE (to docs, reduced to a one-line citation), DELETE, KEEP, DO_NOT_MOVE, or\n      CORRECT-IN-PLACE. CORRECT if it documents current behavior/a live invariant; DELETE only\n      when the referent is gone (record the reason in the commit body).\n- [x] MOOT ITEM (do not re-correct): the `_mcp_models.py` schema-assurance comment is already\n      accurate on current main — it cites the real CI drift gate and `BridgeFsckOut.binding_drift`\n      already exists. Treat it as DO_NOT_MOVE (accurate). Do NOT delete or rewrite it, and do NOT\n      re-file the already-fixed drift defect.\n- [x] DO_NOT_MOVE (verified): `_mcp_llm.py`'s tool docstrings (~121 lines) are the wire-visible\n      MCP tool descriptions FastMCP publishes to clients (API surface, zero recoverable);\n      `_config_schema.py`'s `# read-via:` markers (12 of them) are machine-consumed by the CI gate\n      `scripts/check_config_reads.py` (deleting one breaks CI). Both stay verbatim.\n- [x] `_config_schema.py` documentation caveat (NO doc loss): ~280 of its lines are comments and\n      for many keys they are the ONLY documentation (`docs/config.md` has no rows for\n      `completion_floor_active`, `comment_max_chars`, `auth_proxy_secret_env`, etc). Recover more\n      than the ~34 trivially-recoverable lines ONLY by writing the `docs/config.md` rows FIRST,\n      then relocating; never trim a key's sole documentation.\n- [x] The shard's do_not_move list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` BEFORE any edit lands.\n- [x] Any ADRs proposed from `review_bot/` (bounded shutdown; deploy-safe in-flight counter;\n      retryable coverage-gap deferral) are created only if they document a real current invariant,\n      numbered from the next free ADR id, and cited from the code they explain rather than\n      inlined.\n- [x] The actual recovered comment-line count is measured by diff and recorded on this ticket as\n      an OUTPUT, not a target. No load-bearing invariant is lost.\n- [x] No behaviour change: the full test suite AND `make lint` / `make typecheck` pass unchanged.","id":"7341-c605-e265-4838","parent_id":"f1e2-980c-32ee-4b4d","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Comment triage: root modules and services"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788220170128029001,"uuid":"0544f026-176a-4733-af82-8cd0414f9b4e"}